Z||000000||fogglethorpe||10-13-2001||11:43 AM||||I noticed all you guys have vast knowledge of things technical and mechanical, so let me run this by you...<P>I have a whatchamacallit, the you know what kind, and the thingee broke off the whoosamawhat..anyway, I tried to refasten it with some stuff, and it kinda worked, but now the doohickey on the whatnot is sticking too...I think some of that goo ran down into the whatsit, just enough to clog up the whatever.<P>Have any of you guys ever run into this problem? If so, how did you fix it?<P>------------------<BR>I don't think so;therefore, I'm probably not.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||10-13-2001||12:10 PM||||I hate it when that happens!<BR>It's a write off, Just get another one!||||reg||12
Z||000002||maryjane||10-13-2001||12:25 PM||||Had the same problem with my widget(insignificant part for a useless machine that does nothing in particular) kinda like the print scrn key.<BR>There, Fogelthorpe. I did my part to keep this one from "lanquishing and dying"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||10-13-2001||12:34 PM||||the whatchamacallit on my thingymabobber snapped of, so i took my shirt off and twisted it around my hand like a hellicopter, but that didnt do anything, oh well.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">          <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000004||Coconut||10-13-2001||01:43 PM||||You may have reconglomerated the thingamajig when you refastened the thingee to the whoosamawhat....sometimes we can overlook the obvious in our haste to get something fixed. Try readjusting your whatchamallit so that it will not make contact with the doohickey..part of the problem may be that the whole assembly may be totally miscombobulated!<P>Hope that helps! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||GarethWright||10-13-2001||02:55 PM||||I guess you have one of the older model whatchamacallits, on my '99 model the whatever has a built-in goo filter, and the thingee is not even attached to the whoosamawhat to begin with.  If you have the pre-'98 model you can get a thingamajig from their website (forgot the address) to replace the whole thingee/whoosamawhat assembly, its like $15 and really worth it, even if you haven't had problems yet.  Also, just use a paper towel to clean the goo off of the whatsit and run water through the whatever, flush the system and replace the goo, then get the filter (direct bolt-in) from that website I forgot the addy for, and you should be good to go.  They really should do a recall, but hey, they're just in it for the money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Good luck with it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||10-13-2001||03:16 PM||||i can lend you my duct tape||||reg||1
Z||000007||Kasdan||10-13-2001||03:34 PM||||dont forget to put a new filter on the whatchamacallit after you clean it and put it back on the whatsamahoosel.  If you dont, the thingy will break again, causing the whatever to spew purple goo all over the discombobulated whatsitsname.  you can get the recalled part from gm for a little under a million dollars, its really worth it unless you want another whateveryoucallit breaking.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fogglethorpe||10-13-2001||03:58 PM||||Thanks for all your expertise, guys. I was able to get all the sticky goo out of the thingee, and now the whatever is working. But now, there is some oily, juicy slime running out of that gadget with the spout on it. It only happens when the whatsaname is spinning. Does this mean I should replace the whirly looking affair? Also, is there a manual available for a whatchamacallit?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Kasdan||10-13-2001||04:06 PM||||Yes, there is a manual available, but the numbers are wrong, and chances are more oil would spew from the whatchadoodle, but then again, the whateveritis may be the problem.  try adjusting it.||||reg||1
